// A block-wrap flip (soak nov25b): with the list bound first the function,
// which nothing calls, was refused "cannot compare [i64, duration] with
// List<'_>". The comparison's operand then is a cell of the definition that
// waits on `x`; it was not left to the instances as an operand that holds
// `x` is, and was judged at the input's end over the scheme's own variable.
// It is each call's to judge either way.
// Expected trace (both engines): 1.
{ let f = |x, y| cast<[i64, duration]>("3.0")$ == { let tm__0 = [<0, x>]; tm__0 }; 1 }
